NetHack 3.0 (Pl8) binaries for the PC, Amiga, Mac, and Atari ST are
now available for anonymous ftp from linc.cis.upen.edu, pub/NH3.0/...
Following are the msgs from the porting teams.

Binaries for OS/2 will be made available in a few days (connectivity
problems).

There is an urgent need for a VMS site which allows for anonymous ftp,
and which will be willing to post on pub the VMS NetHack binaries for
public access.  If you know of such a site, please contact Pat Rankin
(nethack.rankin@eql.caltech.edu) who is a member of our VMS porting team.

-Izchak

-------------------------------
IBM PC: The PC Overlaid packages are available by anonymous ftp from
	linc.cis.upenn.edu, pub/NH3.0/PC, and its sub-directories disk1
	and disk2.  For questions about the binaries, contact either
	wizard@chemstor.uoregon.edu, norm@cfctech.cfc.com, or
	stephen@tira.uchicago.edu

Amiga:  For the Amiga, binaries are available by anonymous ftp in the
	pub/NH3.0/amiga directory on linc.cis.upenn.edu [130.91.6.8] and
	in /usenet/comp.binaries.amiga on xanth.cs.odu.edu [128.82.8.1].

	If you cannot ftp, you can request the distribution be sent to 
	you by email.  Send a note to amiga_hack_308@sundown.ebay.sun.com
	and the distribution will be sent to you during off hours.  Note
	that this will trigger a large number of large messages to be 
	sent - you will need almost 700K of spool space to get NetHack 
	this way.  In case of trouble with this method, please drop a note
	to sysadmin@sundown.ebay.sun.com.

	It is also possible to use the ftp/mail service at
	bitftp@pucc.princeton.edu (send a help message to that address for
	further information).

	For other questions about the binaries, please contact either
	keni@dtix.dt.navy.mil or golson@sundown.ebay.sun.com

Mac:	The Macintosh NetHack 3.0 Binary Package, NH3.08.hqx and NH3.08.doc,
	is available by anonymous ftp from:

	apple.com               (130.43.2.2)    pub/nethack
	linc.cis.upenn.edu      (130.91.6.8)    pub/NH3.0/mac

	and should also appear on comp.binaries.mac, soon.

	After a short while the binary package will also appear on various
	popular on-line srevices (GEnie, CompuServe, AppleLink, etc.).  If 
	you are unable to take advantage of these sites and would like to 
	have the package e-mailed contact:  hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu

Atari:  The Atari binaries packages are available by anonymous ftp from
	linc.cis.upenn.edu, pub/NH3.0/atari  For questions about the Atari
	ST binaries, contact Eric Smith (ersmith@uwovax.uwo.ca).


